# React conventions

- Functional components and default exports, matching existing files.
- Pages live in `src/pages/`. Shared UI in `src/components/` (nested folders only when already used, e.g. `footer/`, `about/`).
- Colocate component CSS (`TransporterRow.css` next to `TransporterRow.js`).
- Read/write transporter list and hero titles via `useContext(TransporterContext)`. Pages set `navigationConf` in `useEffect` (see `AboutPage`, `ContactPage`).
- Router: add routes in `src/App.js` as children of `Root`. Use `Link` from `react-router-dom`.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — new global store, English UI, unused route
const [carriers, setCarriers] = useState([]);
<button>Search</button>
<Link to={`/provider/${name}`}>...</Link>

// ✅ GOOD — context + existing Ukrainian copy + real destination
const { transportersList } = useContext(TransporterContext);
<button className="button is-primary">Знайти</button>
<Link to={transporter.url} title="сайт компанії">...</Link>
```

- Prefer small, local `useState`/`useRef` for forms (`ContactUs`). Keep validation in the component unless it is reused.
- `BookCreate.js` / `BookEdit.js` are unused stubs; do not extend them for catalog features.
